  "name": "GAD 65 ANTIBODY FOR TYPE 1 DIABETIES",
  "code": "2011",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<ul>\n<li>Autoantibody against GAD2/GAD65 is seen in pre-diabetics and insulin-dependent (Type I) diabetes mellitus.</li>\n<li>It predicts the rate of progression to insulin requirement in patients affected by Latent Autoimmune Diabetes in Adults&nbsp;&nbsp;(LADA).</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Clinical utility:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>GAD65 antibodies have been associated with a variety of autoimmune neurological syndromes, from stiff person syndrome&nbsp;&nbsp;and cerebellar ataxia to limbic encephalitis (LE) and epilepsy.</li>\n<li>They are a valuable predictor of risk and progression to overt autoimmune diabetes.</li>\n<li>Also useful in distinguishing insulin-dependent from noninsulin dependent diabetics</li>\n<li>Presence of multiple autoantibodies in an individual i.e., GAD-65, ICA, IA-2, IAA, ZnT8 has a very high predictive value for&nbsp;type 1 diabetes.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Note</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>A result within the expected range does not rule out the presence of disease and should be interpreted together with other&nbsp;&nbsp;diagnostic procedures</li>\n</ul>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
